    <h2 class="h1 mb-4">About Beyond SR 513</h2>
    <p>
      Beyond SR 513 is a volunteer-led advocacy effort started by residents of
      northeast Seattle who walk, bike, and take the bus along Sand Point Way NE.  The initiative was convened through the <a href="https://northeast.streetsalliance.org/" target="_blank">Northeast Safe Streets</a> and <a href="https://lakecity.streetsalliance.org/" target="_blank">Lake City Streets Alliance</a>, part of the <a href="https://streetsalliance.org/" target="_blank">Seattle Streets Alliance</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      SR 513 was the state highway designation for this road until the portion from I-5 
      to Magnuson Park was transferred back to the city. 
      The name of our group is a reminder that the road design can move <em>beyond</em> its
      highway-era design.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-0">
      We aim to work with the Seattle Department of Transportation, Seattle City
      Councilmembers, and community organizations to advocate for safe, walkable, and
      bike-accessible streets along this corridor.
    </p>
    <h3 class="h3 mt-4 mb-3">Mission Statement</h3>
    <p>The group aims to work collaboratively with the Seattle Department of Transportation, city council representatives, and local organizations to promote safe, walkable, and bike-accessible streets along Sand Point Way.</p>
  </div>
</section>
